----------------------------------------------------------------------
Python dependencies
----------------------------------------------------------------------

See `pyproject.toml` and `uv.lock` for the authoritative list. Notable
runtime dependencies and their licenses:

  - FastAPI, Pydantic, SQLModel / SQLAlchemy, litellm, arq, Typer / Rich (MIT)
  - httpx, Jinja2, authlib (BSD-3-Clause)
  - structlog (Apache-2.0 / MIT)
  - zaproxy python client (Apache-2.0)
  - PyGithub (LGPL-3.0), python-gvm (GPL-3.0), shodan (MIT)

----------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party software inside the Docker images
----------------------------------------------------------------------

The images published as `roqueribeiro1988/roqueos-shield` (engine, tag
`vX.Y.Z`) and `...-standalone` (all-in-one, tag `vX.Y.Z-standalone`) bundle
the following third-party programs and data, unmodified, each under its own
license. Their source is available from the upstream projects.

Engine image (docker/images/orchestrator/Dockerfile):

  - Nmap (Debian package)            Nmap Public Source License
  - nuclei                           MIT
  - nuclei-templates                 MIT
  - gitleaks                         MIT
  - trufflehog                       AGPL-3.0
  - trivy                            Apache-2.0
  - semgrep (engine)                 LGPL-2.1
  - semgrep-rules                    Semgrep Rules License v1.0
  - checkov                          Apache-2.0
  - Debian packages (base image)     their respective licenses
  - Python 3.13                      PSF License

Standalone image (docker/images/standalone/Dockerfile), in addition:

  - OWASP ZAP                        Apache-2.0
  - Redis (Debian package)           BSD-3-Clause
  - OpenJDK 21 JRE (Debian package)  GPL-2.0 with Classpath Exception
  - Firefox ESR (Debian package)     MPL-2.0

The scanners are run as separate programs; RoqueShield does not link against
them.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
Lab targets (not redistributed)
----------------------------------------------------------------------

The `lab` profile of `docker/compose.yml` references intentionally vulnerable
third-party applications (OWASP Juice Shop, DVWA, WebGoat). They are pulled at
runtime from their official registries and are not part of this distribution.
